<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6099" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caesĭus</span></b> , i,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a Roman cognomen.</i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> M. Caesius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				13, 11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Another M. Caesius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 1, 50, §
			130</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> P. Caesius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Balb. 22,
			50</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			Sex. Caesius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 28,
			68</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>V.</b>
			Caesius Bassus, <i>the friend to whom Persius addressed
				his sixth satire;</i> cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 10,
				1, 96</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
